2. **Apply Leibniz's rule**: Express $\frac{d}{d\nu}f(\nu)$ as the sum of (a) $\int_{\arcsin \nu}^{\pi/2} \frac{\partial}{\partial \nu} \left( \frac{1}{\sqrt{\sin^2 \theta - \nu^2}} \right) d\theta$ and (b) the boundary term $\frac{d}{d\nu}(\arcsin \nu) \cdot \lim_{\theta \to \arcsin \nu^+} \frac{1}{\sqrt{\sin^2 \theta - \nu^2}}$.  
