2. Determine the residual mass in the exact chiral symmetry limit: recognize that both contributions vanish except for electroweak effects, which are constrained to <0.5% of the physical mass. 
3. Compute the percentage decrease using the formula [(100% - residual mass percentage)], leveraging the <0.5% upper bound for residual mass to confirm the decrease exceeds 99.5%. 
4. Map the result to the answer choice range 99.5–100%.
