2. Define a new function \( g(x) = f(x) - 2547 \). Then we can rewrite the given functional equation in terms of \( g \):
   \[
   f(x + y) = f(x) + f(y) + 2547
   \]
   Substituting \( f(x) = g(x) + 2547 \) and \( f(y) = g(y) + 2547 \) into the equation, we get:
   \[
   g(x + y) + 2547 = (g(x) + 2547) + (g(y) + 2547) + 2547
   \]
   Simplifying this, we have:
   \[
   g(x + y) + 2547 = g(x) + g(y) + 3 \cdot 2547
   \]
   \[
   g(x + y) = g(x) + g(y)
   \]
